he's Kurt Warner he's a hall-of-famer  NFL Network analyst former Super Bowl  MVP you can see Kurt Warner every Sunday  on NFL gameday morning at 9:00 Eastern  Kurt thanks for joining us good morning  your reaction when you heard the Giants  were benching Eli Manning good morning I  was disappointed I think like a lot of  people were disappointed and just the  nature of of how it went down and the  season that they had and all the things  that have gone sideways you know I kind  of expected something like this to  happen to to kind of point out Eli and  you know I just feel like sometimes you  make and put the blame on one guy and  that's what this is that they've had so  many things go bad he's out there  competing and then to make the statement  well Eli Manning's still our quarterback  well he's still your quarterback to me  he deserves to start he deserves to  compete he deserves a chance to be out  there with these guys trying to win  every football game and then I would  have no problem if they said well this  thing goes sideways now we're try to  dabble with it these young guys and see  if we feel they can be a backup to Eli  Manning or the next guy when Eli decides  to retire but to kind of put it out  there like this like hey you can start  when we'll save the streak but but know  that you're not going to finish this  game or you're not going to have a  chance to go the full distance with your  guys we're gonna put these other guys in  I just I didn't like the nature of how  they did it and what they said that they  were with it but also if you're looking  at this I think people have a problem  that you're gonna bench Eli and you're  gonna bring in Geno Smith and say that  you know we want to continue to win  games but we want to take inventory of  these other quarterbacks if Davis Webb  was getting the starting nod I think  people would have less of a problem with  this Kurt you agree yeah I agree you  know I think you know a lot of people  are gonna look and say well Gino had his  opportunities we kind of know what Gino  is we don't know what Davis Webb is but  again I think it's the nature of if we  believe if this Webb is the future and  it's not Eli Manning that to me is  different if you say hey we have to move  and play towards the future that's one  thing but to say well Eli's our  quarterback but that to me is the thing  that's a bit I mean if he's  and you're ready to move on then just  say that and put it out there and let it  be what it is and I think a lot of  people at that point might not be happy  with it or might not agree with it but  at least at that point you go okay this  makes sense that we can you know take  these last few games and see what our  future is because Eli's not our future  but they come out and say yeah yeah he's  still our guy and then as you said to  start Gino instead of Davis yeah just a  lot of curious things and sometimes you  just want to just come out and say what  it is and let us know and you respect  people a lot more when they do that as  opposed to you know kind of going around  in circles and everybody trying to  figure out what what are you really  trying to do here  how were you told back in November of  2004 that Eli was going to be the  starter and you lost your job  what a great respect for Tom Coughlin  because of how he told me he brought me  into his office and we sat down and you  know at the time you know we were a  playoff team we were five and four but  we had dropped a couple games and and he  basically just looked me in the eye and  said Kurt we're going to replace your  quarterback and it really has nothing to  do with how you played and you know  we're in a great position now but I feel  like I have to make this move for the  organization and for the future I have  to start the future right now and you  know I'm sorry it's not fair but that's  what I feel like I need to do and for me  I greatly respected him I didn't agree  with it you know you always want to  believe we're the best guy for the job  should have the job at that point but he  was honest with me and said this is a  move for the future and I just feel like  this is the right timing and  unfortunately you're the one that gets  affected by it but you know I just have  to do what I feel is right and I'm left  there with so much respect for the man  because he looked me in the eye and he  didn't make excuses he didn't try to  blame me or you know or say something  that wasn't the truth he just laid it  out there and and we move forward if Tom  Coughlin was still the coach with the  Giants would this have happened I don't  think there's any chance this happens  knowing Tom Coughlin and what he  believes in and the kind of man that he  is I think he would you know even if you  know you look back at the game and say  well Eli wasn't playing at Eli level and  I can agree with that but again you have  to take the big  go well it was because Eli isn't good  enough anymore is it  or is it because of everything else that  went sideways and I just think Tom's you  know just out of respect for the  situation and as a head coach saying  we're gonna go down and we're gonna  compete and I see that this isn't just  about Eli so it will affect the streak  and the effect what he's meant to our  organization when I know there's a lot  of things going on I don't think Tom  would have made that same decision  he's Kurt Warner hall-of-famer NFL  Network analyst you can see him every  Sunday morning NFL game day morning  starting at 9:00 a.m. Eastern Jimmy  Garoppolo finally gets the start in San  Francisco why did it take this long I  think it just took this long because  you're trying to put him in a position  where he's got enough of a handle on  things that he could succeed you have to  look as an organization when you made  this move you knew this was a move for  the long term but you didn't have to  rush it so it didn't look like you  wanted it to look early and so you know  with Beathard playing decent and getting  that first win I think it bought them a  little bit more time for Jimmy to just  get more comfortable with things but  this was inevitable we knew this was  going to happen at some point this year  with the record but some of those  performances I think where they were  competitive or they won a game allowed  them to say ok Jimmy gets another week  so when he gets in there he can be as  comfortable as possible and have success  because that's really what they need  they need everybody to see this was the  right move here's why and it puts Jimmy  in a great situation to succeed from the  get-go if you're Andy Reed do you make a  quarter vacuum change well I mean it's a  tough one I don't make the team I love  Ellen and I think Alex Smith is a really  really good quarterback and better than  most guys in this league you know the it  always comes down to the idea of are we  here to win championships and do we to  believe Alex Smith can win us a  championship and you know the first  whatever five six games of the year  everybody was watching him and going oh  my gosh this this guy is awesome can do  everything you know he can win a  championship with this team and now all  of a sudden we saw word on that a little  bit but that to me is that is the  question  is that that's what we play for and you  know we've had a lot of questions about  Alec Smith and the game manager and all  that stuff and if Andy Reid feels like  he can only take us so far and we  probably won't win a championship with  Alec Smith now you have to consider to  me the next move in the future I don't  believe that I believe Alex would be so  much better than that you're gonna give  it out in their homes right now and for  this season but I just believe that's  the question you have to ask because  alex is a really really good quarterback  a starting quarterback that has done a  lot of great things he has yet to prove  that he can win a championship but not  to me is the only question that you have  Kurt thanks for joining us have a great  weekend that's a Kurt Warner for more  Dan Patrick show to the audience channel  239 on DirecTV or download the Dan  Patrick show at  [Music]

